---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ORG_ID } from '../lib/agent/jsonld';
import { CONTACT, SITE } from '../lib/agent/site';

const updated = '2026-10-08';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Rowhouse privacy policy',
  url: `${SITE.url}/privacy`,
  dateModified: updated,
  publisher: { '@id': ORG_ID },
};

const linkClass = 'text-accent-hi underline decoration-accent/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-accent-hi';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy | Rowhouse"
  description="What Rowhouse collects, why, and what it never records. Your microphone audio is fingerprinted on your device and discarded; the film never leaves your room."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-12 sm:px-6">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent-hi">Privacy · updated {updated}</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl leading-[1.05] text-text-hi sm:text-5xl">
      We listen for ten seconds. We keep none of it.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-text-mid">
      Rowhouse needs your microphone to find your place in a film, and an account if you want to
      chat, follow creators, or publish commentary. This page lists everything we store, why, and
      who else touches it. No ads, no tracking pixels, no selling data.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-text-dim">01. Your microphone</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl text-text-hi">Audio never leaves your device.</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-text-mid">
        When you sync, the browser captures about ten seconds of room audio. It's turned into a
        fingerprint, a set of hashes of spectral peaks, right there on your device, matched against
        the film's map, and discarded. We don't record it, upload it, or store it. That rule is
        enforced in the code and guarded by an automated test in the open-source sync engine.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-text-dim">02. Your account</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl text-text-hi">The minimum to know it's you.</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-text-mid">
        You can browse and listen without signing in. If you sign in with Google, we store your email
        address, display name, profile picture URL, a public handle, and the Google account ID that
        links them. A sign-in session is a random token kept in an HttpOnly cookie for up to 30 days;
        we store only a hash of it. Two short-lived cookies protect the sign-in handshake and expire
        after ten minutes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-text-dim">03. What you do here</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl text-text-hi">The things you choose to share.</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-text-mid">
        We store the creators you follow, watchlist votes, reports you file, and, if you're a creator,
        your bio, the commentary audio you upload, and the fingerprint maps built from it. Live chat
        messages are stored with your display name so late arrivals can scroll back; each room keeps
        only its most recent 500. Reactions are stored as anonymous timestamps on the track. If you
        turn on notifications, we keep your browser's push subscription so we can tell you when a
        creator goes live.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-text-dim">04. Who else is involved</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl text-text-hi">A short list of processors.</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-text-mid">
        Rowhouse runs on Cloudflare, which hosts the site, database, and audio storage and processes
        standard request data such as IP addresses to serve and protect it. Google handles sign-in.
        Film posters load from TMDB's image servers, so your browser contacts them directly. Push
        notifications are delivered by your browser vendor's push service. We don't use analytics or
        advertising services.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 mb-4">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-text-dim">05. Your choices</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl text-text-hi">Ask, and it's gone.</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-text-mid">
        You can sign out at any time, which deletes your session. To get a copy of your data or have
        your account and everything attached to it deleted,{' '}
        {CONTACT.email ? (
          <>email <a class={linkClass} href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.</>
        ) : (
          <>reach us through the <a class={linkClass} href="/contact">contact page</a>.</>
        )}{' '}
        Rowhouse isn't directed at children under 13. If this policy changes, we'll update the date
        at the top of this page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
